e. be involved in every stage of the development process; f. be free from slavery or servitude;g. be free from threats;
h. obtain protection of her person, family, honor, dignity and property rights;
i. obtain welfare and a decent life; j. participate in the political, economic, socio-cultural fields;
k. perform legal acts; andl. freely choose a partner in her marriage. (2) Every wife during the marriage bond has equal rights and responsibilities with her husband over all matters relating to their married life, relations with their children, and ownership and management of joint property in accordance with applicable laws and regulations. (3) After the dissolution of marriage, a woman has rights and responsibilities with her former husband over all matters relating to children with due regard to the best interests of the child.

Article 20

1. In implementing protection services for women, the Regional Government establishes P2TP2A as a service network for women victims of violence.
2. The establishment of P2TP2A is intended so that women victims of violence obtain comprehensive, integrated, quality, inclusive and sustainable services.
3. P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) has the following duties: a. providing services to women victims of violence in accordance with standard operating procedures; b. coordinating prevention, services and referrals among government-owned service institutions, community-owned service institutions, professional organizations, law enforcement agencies and other related institutions;
c. conducting data collection on case services;
d. providing various information needed by victims, victims' families and the community;
e. conducting prevention of recurrence of violence, exploitation and discrimination against women; f. conducting monitoring and evaluation of victim services; and g. providing capacity strengthening, guidance and assistance related to victim services.

Article 23

1. Services are implemented to fulfill the rights of women victims of violence and are carried out with the following principles: a. respect for human rights; b. non-discrimination;
c. confidentiality;
d. empathy;
e. inclusion;
f. empowerment;
g. victim-based decisions;
h. honesty;
i. professionalism;
j. integration; and k. sustainability.
2. Services to women victims of violence must consider special conditions and needs based on the vulnerability experienced by women as referred to in Article 20

REGENT OF MAMUJU

WEST SULAWESI PROVINCE

REGIONAL REGULATION OF MAMUJU REGENCY

NUMBER 9 OF 2023

CONCERNING

EMPOWERMENT AND PROTECTION OF WOMEN

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

THE REGENT OF MAMUJU,

Considering:
a. that the fulfillment of constitutional rights and protection of women's human rights regarding empowerment and protection of women is one of the values contained in Pancasila and the 1945 Constitution;
b. that women play a very important role in the process of continuation and creation of quality generations, thus requiring a sense of security, obtaining guarantees of protection from acts of violence and discrimination, and need to be empowered so that they can actualize their potential optimally;
c. that based on Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government as mentioned in the Appendix, it is stated that the division of government affairs in the field of women's empowerment with one of the sub-affairs is the protection of women;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Empowerment and Protection of Women;

In View of:
1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 29 of 1959 concerning the Establishment of Level II Regions in Sulawesi (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1959 Number 74, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1822);
3. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended several times most recently by Law Number 6 of 2023 concerning the Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 2 of 2022 concerning Job Creation into Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2023 Number 41, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6856);
4. Law Number 12 of 2022 concerning the Criminal Act of Sexual Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2022 Number 120, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6792);

With the Mutual Approval of THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF MAMUJU REGENCY and

Article 4

1. To improve the quality of life of women, the Regional Government is responsible for:a. respecting and guaranteeing women's rights without discrimination in accordance with human dignity;
b. institutionalization of Gender Mainstreaming in Regional Government institutions; c. Women's Empowerment;
d. strengthening and developing Women's Empowerment service provider institutions in the Region.
2. Efforts to improve the quality of life of women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by Regional Apparatus that administer governmental affairs in the field of women's empowerment and child protection.

Article 27

1. Social rehabilitation services as referred to in Article 24 paragraph (1) letter c shall be implemented with the following activities:a. counseling;
b. assistance;
c. linguists and/or translators;
d. spiritual guidance;
e. shelter and/or safe house;
f. temporary shelter;
g. strengthening based on family and/or group support;
h. mobility support for victims with disabilities;
i. provision of special social assistance for victims; and j. other forms of social rehabilitation services needed by victims.
2. Social rehabilitation services as referred to in paragraph (1) letters a, b, c, d, f, g, h, and i shall be the responsibility of the Regional Apparatus in charge of women's empowerment and child protection affairs.
3. Social rehabilitation services as referred to in paragraph (1) letters e and j shall be the responsibility of the Regional Apparatus in charge of social affairs and women's empowerment and child protection affairs.
4. Further provisions regarding social rehabilitation services shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

