Article 20

1. In implementing protection services for women, the Regional Government establishes P2TP2A as a service network for women victims of violence.
2. The establishment of P2TP2A is intended so that women victims of violence obtain comprehensive, integrated, quality, inclusive and sustainable services.
3. P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) has the following duties: a. providing services to women victims of violence in accordance with standard operating procedures; b. coordinating prevention, services and referrals among government-owned service institutions, community-owned service institutions, professional organizations, law enforcement agencies and other related institutions;
c. conducting data collection on case services;
d. providing various information needed by victims, victims' families and the community;
e. conducting prevention of recurrence of violence, exploitation and discrimination against women; f. conducting monitoring and evaluation of victim services; and g. providing capacity strengthening, guidance and assistance related to victim services.

Article 27

1. Social rehabilitation services as referred to in Article 24 paragraph (1) letter c shall be implemented with the following activities:a. counseling;
b. assistance;
c. linguists and/or translators;
d. spiritual guidance;
e. shelter and/or safe house;
f. temporary shelter;
g. strengthening based on family and/or group support;
h. mobility support for victims with disabilities;
i. provision of special social assistance for victims; and j. other forms of social rehabilitation services needed by victims.
2. Social rehabilitation services as referred to in paragraph (1) letters a, b, c, d, f, g, h, and i shall be the responsibility of the Regional Apparatus in charge of women's empowerment and child protection affairs.
3. Social rehabilitation services as referred to in paragraph (1) letters e and j shall be the responsibility of the Regional Apparatus in charge of social affairs and women's empowerment and child protection affairs.
4. Further provisions regarding social rehabilitation services shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

Article 4

1. To improve the quality of life of women, the Regional Government is responsible for:a. respecting and guaranteeing women's rights without discrimination in accordance with human dignity;
b. institutionalization of Gender Mainstreaming in Regional Government institutions; c. Women's Empowerment;
d. strengthening and developing Women's Empowerment service provider institutions in the Region.
2. Efforts to improve the quality of life of women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by Regional Apparatus that administer governmental affairs in the field of women's empowerment and child protection.

Article 34

Counseling as referred to in Article 32 letter b includes:
a. providing protection and assistance to develop oneself through improving family capabilities and skills;
b. conducting outreach on improving women's quality of life;
c. conducting outreach on improving gender equality in community family life;
d. increasing access and opportunities to receive information and economic resources through efforts to increase prosperous family income and increase women's economic productivity; ande. making efforts to empower female heads of households.

Article 12

Women's empowerment in the social field shall be implemented through;
a. increasing knowledge, attitudes and skills to encourage the fulfillment of tiered education according to potential to improve social status;
b. increasing awareness, willingness and ability to overcome health problems through quality promotive, preventive, curative, and rehabilitative efforts, especially in the field of reproductive health;
c. increasing awareness and knowledge about independent, healthy and prosperous family planning including access to consultation services and marriage registration; andd. facilitation and efforts to preserve customs and develop science, technology, arts and culture for the advancement of women.

